  "answer": "Traditional support lookup tasks in this corpus are direct, natural-language lookup queries. The golden dataset for validation splits queries as \"40% direct lookup\" [NL-008#NL-008-S08], and TutorChat supports patterns such as Policy Lookup, Onboarding Procedures, Troubleshooting Assistance, and Course Verification [NL-028#NL-028-S06]. These queries are processed through semantic query processing, vector retrieval, permission filtering, and grounded answer generation with inline citations [NL-002#NL-002-S02].\n\nStructured BI-style questions are instead represented as SQL retrieval targets against tabular data. The support report aligns with the `support_tickets` table and supports aggregations such as `SELECT category, SUM(ticket_count) ... GROUP BY category`, average ticket counts by segment, SLA bottleneck queries for high-severity open tickets older than 48 hours, and average CSAT scores by plan tier [NL-029#NL-029-S07].\n\nIn short, traditional support lookups ask TutorChat to retrieve and synthesize grounded document evidence, while structured BI-style questions ask the system to compute aggregate metrics from structured ticket and satisfaction tables.\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer\nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
